From 38075c86641347673a6ea0ee8dc9360a5de1b264 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:32:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Show a report's diagram on the landing page

The landing page gains "The report", after "How it works": what bcr
report shows, a static picture of one of its diagrams to illustrate
it, and a link to its documentation; no link to a live report. The
picture sits on a light card in both colour schemes. specs/site claims
the new heading, allows pictures that illustrate as long as they are
real bcr report output, and checks that each picture is in
site/static with alt text; pages.yml runs that check.

docs/bcr.md and README.md no longer say GitHub draws the diagrams
wherever it shows Markdown: release notes show them as code, as
checked in a draft release. docs/bcr.1 is generated again.

site/static/report-filter.png is not in this patch: take the
screenshot the PBI describes and add it to the same commit.

- PBI-00039: this change.
- site: the seventh section, pictures, and the picture guardrail.

Verify with: go test ./internal/manpage, the pipe in AGENTS.md's
Toolchain, and the spec's Regression Guardrails on a build with the
pinned Hugo

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JQNYCuXgGxwDyisZpL318X
